  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The modulation index of an amplitude modulated signal is defined as the measure or extent of amplitude variation about an un-modulated carrier.</p><p>Modulation index is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>To&nbsp;avoid distortion,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;because &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;will result in interference between career frequency and message frequency,&nbsp;resulting into distortion.&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
